{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VfPSt1iFktTie3ax1a7PkG","type":"tool_result","content":"analysis/roster.json\nanalysis/roster.json.prov.json\nanalysis/derived_metrics.json\nanalysis/derived_metrics.json.prov.json\nanalysis/evaluator_snapshot/plane_config.json\nanalysis/evaluator_snapshot/evaluate_final.py\nsource_evidence/downstream/baseline/program_spec.toml\nsource_evidence/downstream/program/program_spec.toml\nsource_evidence/downstream/baseline/src/program.py\nsource_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Starter candidate: log-linear ridge regression of cover time on six graph statistics.\n     2\t\n     3\tInterface (``python_rpc_v1:handle``): ``handle(request) -> response`` over finite,\n     4\tJSON-compatible values only (no NaN/Infinity, no files, no paths). The evaluator and\n     5\tthis candidate share no filesystem; all inputs arrive inline in the request.\n     6\t\n     7\tEpisode transcript (identical in smoke, search and final; exactly one episode per reset):\n     8\t\n     9\t1. ``{\"op\": \"reset\", \"seed\": int}`` -> ``{\"ok\": True}`` (exactly this one key).\n    10\t   Clears all state. ``seed`` is any non-negative integer and only seeds candidate-internal\n    11\t   randomness; it never identifies the plane, data or workload.\n    12\t   Timeout: 5 s (includes process start and imports).\n    13\t\n    14\t2. ``{\"op\": \"fit\", \"feature_names\": [str]*6, \"X\": [[float]*6]*N_train, \"y\": [float]*N_train,\n    15\t   \"y_se\": [float]*N_train, \"n_walks\": int}`` -> ``{\"ok\": True}`` with optional\n    16\t   ``\"method\": str`` (<= 256 chars). No other keys are allowed.\n    17\t   ``feature_names`` is ``[\"n\", \"m\", \"mean_degree\", \"max_degree\", \"min_degree\", \"diameter\"]``\n    18\t   (mean_degree = 2m/n, diameter by BFS). Each row of ``X`` describes one connected graph\n    19\t   with 5 <= n <= 30 from the training pool. ``y`` is the evaluator's Monte Carlo estimate of\n    20\t   the uniform-start expected cover time (steps until a simple random walk, started at a\n    21\t   uniformly random vertex, has visited every vertex), ``y_se`` its standard error, and\n    22\t   ``n_walks`` the number of walks per label. N_train is conveyed only by the row count\n    23\t   (roughly 20-130). Timeout: 45 s.\n    24\t\n    25\t3. ``{\"op\": \"predict\", \"X\": [[float]*6]*N}`` -> ``{\"pred\": [float]*N}`` (exactly this one key):\n    26\t   one strictly positive finite predicted expected cover time per row, in request order.\n    27\t   Each episode issues exactly three predict calls after fit, on held-out graphs (rows may\n    28\t   be reordered or re-paired between calls); predictions should be a pure function of the\n    29\t   six statistics of each row. Timeout: 10 s per call.\n    30\t\n    31\tAny other response shape (wrong keys, wrong length, non-numeric or non-finite values, an\n    32\texception) fails the whole episode. Non-positive predictions are scored as worst case.\n    33\tScoring (evaluator-side): per-graph error min(|ln pred - ln C|, ln 1000), averaged per graph\n    34\tfamily with equal family weights; lower error is better. Requests never contain graph\n    35\tidentifiers, family labels, adjacency, held-out labels or scores.\n    36\t\"\"\"\n    37\t\n    38\timport math\n    39\t\n    40\timport numpy as np\n    41\t\n    42\t_STATE = {}\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\tdef _design(X):\n    46\t    X = np.asarray(X, dtype=float)\n    47\t    n, m, mean_deg, max_deg, min_deg, diam = (X[:, i] for i in range(6))\n    48\t    cols = [np.ones(len(X)), np.log(n), np.log(m), np.log(mean_deg), np.log(max_deg),\n    49\t            np.log(min_deg), np.log(diam), np.log(n) * np.log(diam)]\n    50\t    return np.column_stack(cols)\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\tdef _reset(request):\n    54\t    seed = request.get(\"seed\")\n    55\t    if type(seed) is not int or seed < 0:\n    56\t        raise ValueError(\"invalid seed\")\n    57\t    _STATE.clear()\n    58\t    _STATE[\"seed\"] = seed\n    59\t    return {\"ok\": True}\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\tdef _fit(request):\n    63\t    A = _design(request[\"X\"])\n    64\t    y = np.log(np.asarray(request[\"y\"], dtype=float))\n    65\t    mu = A[:, 1:].mean(axis=0)\n    66\t    sd = A[:, 1:].std(axis=0)\n    67\t    sd[sd < 1e-12] = 1.0\n    68\t    Z = np.column_stack([A[:, 0], (A[:, 1:] - mu) / sd])\n    69\t    ridge = 1e-3 * np.eye(Z.shape[1])\n    70\t    ridge[0, 0] = 0.0\n    71\t    beta = np.linalg.solve(Z.T @ Z + ridge, Z.T @ y)\n    72\t    _STATE.update(mu=mu, sd=sd, beta=beta, fallback=float(y.mean()))\n    73\t    return {\"ok\": True, \"method\": \"ridge_log_linear_v0\"}\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\tdef _predict(request):\n    77\t    if \"beta\" not in _STATE:\n    78\t        raise RuntimeError(\"predict before fit\")\n    79\t    A = _design(request[\"X\"])\n    80\t    Z = np.column_stack([A[:, 0], (A[:, 1:] - _STATE[\"mu\"]) / _STATE[\"sd\"]])\n    81\t    log_pred = np.clip(Z @ _STATE[\"beta\"], -50.0, 50.0)\n    82\t    log_pred = np.where(np.isfinite(log_pred), log_pred, _STATE[\"fallback\"])\n    83\t    return {\"pred\": [float(math.exp(v)) for v in log_pred]}\n    84\t\n    85\t\n    86\tdef handle(request):\n    87\t    op = request.get(\"op\") if isinstance(request, dict) else None\n    88\t    if op == \"reset\":\n    89\t        return _reset(request)\n    90\t    if op == \"fit\":\n    91\t        return _fit(request)\n    92\t    if op == \"predict\":\n    93\t        return _predict(request)\n    94\t    raise ValueError(\"unknown op\")","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67ee5d0a-908e-40a8-a0f6-1aad3920c0a7","uuid":"6f27cc24-f167-439c-82f8-a2718f230d3d","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:55:03.244Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"analysis/roster.json\nanalysis/roster.json.prov.json\nanalysis/derived_metrics.json\nanalysis/derived_metrics.json.prov.json\nanalysis/evaluator_snapshot/plane_co